	(footprint "FoveaCamDuo:PinHeader_1x10_P1.27mm_Horizontal_Box"
		(layer "B.Cu")
		(uuid "64a79767-26e1-48a9-80ba-4c0cc22a3eac")
		(at 28.1 -4.572 90)
		(descr "Drill 0.68 mm finished (owner 2026-10-07: V0.0's 0.762 felt loose; CNC Tech allows 0.70 +/-0.05; pin SQ0.40 +/-0.02, diagonal <= 0.594; at JLCPCB -0.08 the hole is >= 0.60, at Advanced the order requests +/-0.003 in, >= 0.604); ring (1.06 - 0.68) / 2 = 0.19 mm. Body and courtyard 2026-10-07 from the current CNC Tech drawing 3220-XX-0200-00_.pdf (05-FEB-2020, https://www.cnctech.us/pdfs/3220-XX-0200-00_.pdf): housing 12.70 long, 4.90 deep, rear face 1.00 behind the near (even) row, so the mating face is 5.90 from it; drill 0.70 (recommended hole); silk outline dropped (the body sticks out of the board edge). Pad positions and 3D model reference extracted the footprint embedded as J_SPI1 in the original hand-drawn FoveaCamDuo-PCB.kicad_pcb (KiCad 9, git 289fb6c); not in the stock KiCad 10 library. Original library id: Connector_PinHeader_1.27mm:PinHeader_1x10_P1.27mm_Horizontal_Box. 3D model 2026-10-07: CNC Tech 3220-10-0200-00 manufacturer STEP, unmodified (https://www.cnctech.us/pdfs/3220-10-0200-00%203D.ZIP, linked from https://www.cnctech.us/productdetails.asp?ID=2227; matches the current drawing https://www.cnctech.us/pdfs/3220-XX-0200-00_.pdf, 05-FEB-2020: housing 12.70 x 4.90 deep x 5.0 high, rear face 0.80 to the near tail edge = 1.00 to the near row centre, mating face 5.90 from the near (even) row, tails 2.4, key slot in the wall away from the board). Pads 2026-10-07: 1.06 mm round (1.016 in v0.1.0, 1.07 earlier in v0.1.1): plated ring 0.18 mm, exactly JLCPCB's 2-layer 1 oz PTH minimum (fab review F4), and 0.21 mm copper space between pins >= the owner's 0.008 in (0.2032 mm) floor (owner 2026-10-07, \"Outer Min Space 0.008\"); with the 0.70 mm drill of the CNC Tech drawing a 1.27 mm grid allows at most 1.0668 mm (ring 0.183, space 0.2032), so the ring sits at the minimum by design. Solder mask 2026-10-07 (Advanced PCB standard spec, owner \"Use standard spec\"): one gang opening per face over all ten pads (filled rectangles on F.Mask / B.Mask, pad field + 0.0762 mm), no mask web between the pins: at 1.27 mm pitch the 0.20 mm copper gap cannot hold a web >= 0.1016 mm (Advanced) or 0.13 mm (JLCPCB black) once each pad keeps the 0.0762 mm mask clearance Advanced's standard spec needs; the pads use the board expansion; attribute allow_soldermask_bridges marks the gang opening as intended for KiCad DRC.")
